// ---------- the profiles of the activities that are not their room ----------
// `like`: the scene is played as the citizens' square (the people, the moves and the words of the market) · `roles`: the two guests ([label] or [male, female] when the grammar of the role says the
// gender) · `affiliation`: 'none' (people of other forces or of no party: no label of the player's party on them) · `families`: the topics that make sense for the activity · `voice`: the stance lines
// · `lines`: the questions of the profile in place of the ones of the family · `approaches`: the three ways in (same functions as the kind) · `moves`: the moves of the moments of decision (in place of
// the ones of the kind and of the topic) · `setting` / `place`: the room the scene is drawn in.
